page RecipeNotFoundPage(path: "/recipes/not-found-page", title: "Show your own page for an unknown address — Recipes", description: "Show your own page for an address no page answers: a page whose path is *, kept out of search, and written to 404.html by a static build.") {
    RecipeShell("Show your own page for an unknown address", summary: "A mistyped link or a page that moved should land on a page that says so and offers a way on, not on a blank screen or the host's own error. A page whose `path` is `*` answers every address no other page does:", outputs: ["website", "app"], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [Anchor(id: "how-it-works", label: "How it works"), Anchor(id: "variations", label: "Variations")], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Make a PDF report", to: "/recipes/pdf-report"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Serve a site with nginx", to: "/recipes/serve-with-nginx"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Serve a site with Apache", to: "/recipes/serve-with-apache")], source: "md-docs/recipes/not-found-page.md", how: true, hasVariations: true, project: { "src/pages/NotFoundPage.wf": #"page NotFound(path: "*", title: "Page not found", description: "There is no page at this address.", noindex: true) {
    Heading("We couldn't find that page").h1
    Text("The address may be mistyped, or the page may have moved.")
    Link("Go to the front page", to: "/")
}

page Front(path: "/", title: "Front", description: "The front page.") {
    Heading("Front").h1
    Link("A link to nowhere", to: "/no-such-page")
}
"#, "webfluent.app.json": #"{
  "name": "not-found-page"
}
"# }) {
        code {
            Markdown("**Needs:** nothing besides the page. A static build (`\"ssg\": true`) also writes it to `build/404.html`, which the host must serve for an unknown path: the host recipes below show how.")
            CodeBlock(#"page NotFound(path: "*", title: "Page not found", description: "There is no page at this address.", noindex: true) {
    Heading("We couldn't find that page").h1
    Text("The address may be mistyped, or the page may have moved.")
    Link("Go to the front page", to: "/")
}

page Front(path: "/", title: "Front", description: "The front page.") {
    Heading("Front").h1
    Link("A link to nowhere", to: "/no-such-page")
}"#, title: "wf")
        }
        variations {
            Markdown("- **Say which address was asked for**: a static `404.html` is served at every unknown address, so read the address in the browser, from a project script (`function currentPath() \{ return location.pathname; \}` in `src/path.js`), and show it with `Text(\"No page at \{currentPath()\}.\")`. The text is filled in when the page's script runs.")

        }
        Markdown("`Front` is there so the example has somewhere to go back to; in your project, keep your own `/` page and add only `NotFound` (in `src/pages/NotFound.wf`). Open `/no-such-page` and the router draws `NotFound`.\n\n- `path: \"*\"` matches any address. The router tries the other pages first — static paths, then paths with a `:param` — and `*` last, so it never hides a real page, wherever it is declared.\n- `noindex: true` keeps the page out of search results and out of the sitemap.\n- In a **single-page build** (the default), the router draws `NotFound` for any unknown address once the app has loaded. The host has to send `index.html` for an address it has no file for, so the app loads at all: that is the single-page fallback in [Serve a site with nginx](/recipes/serve-with-nginx), [Apache](/recipes/serve-with-apache) and [Caddy](/recipes/serve-with-caddy).\n- In a **static build** (`\"build\": \{ \"ssg\": true \}`), the build also writes the page as `build/404.html`, with its title and text already in the HTML. GitHub Pages, Netlify and Cloudflare Pages serve `404.html` for a path they have no file for, with the status 404; nginx and Apache do once their config names it (`error_page 404 /404.html;`, `ErrorDocument 404 /404.html`).\n- `wf serve` draws the page for an unknown address too, so you can see it while you work.\n\nCheck the site's own links before you add the `*` page. `wf check` reports a `Link(to:)` or `navigate()` whose path no page's route matches as `R01`, but once a page answers `*`, every path matches it, and that check has nothing left to report.")

    }
}
